  "segments": [
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0001",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "NURSE",
      "start_seconds": 0.85,
      "end_seconds": 9.89,
      "duration_seconds": 9.04,
      "text": "doctor the patient's with us now. I did the usual checks at the front so so just say when you want them"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0002",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 11.8,
      "end_seconds": 15.35,
      "duration_seconds": 3.55,
      "text": "perfect, thanks. Hello there, so what's the trouble?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0003",
      "speaker_id": "person_3",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 16.33,
      "end_seconds": 23.26,
      "duration_seconds": 6.93,
      "text": "um um so... pain in the lower left tummy. That's why I came"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0004",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 24.52,
      "end_seconds": 27.64,
      "duration_seconds": 3.12,
      "text": "Is there any regular medication you use?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0005",
      "speaker_id": "person_3",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 29.09,
      "end_seconds": 31.63,
      "duration_seconds": 2.54,
      "text": "No, I'm not on anything."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0006",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 48.78,
      "end_seconds": 55.76,
      "duration_seconds": 6.98,
      "text": "so, how long has it been like this? I'm asking so that we don't miss anything"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0007",
      "speaker_id": "person_3",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 56.63,
      "end_seconds": 62.0,
      "duration_seconds": 5.37,
      "text": "I'd say six months. Actually, no, closer to two months."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0008",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 63.91,
      "end_seconds": 73.3,
      "duration_seconds": 9.39,
      "text": "tell me a bit more about it: how bad it gets, how often, and whether anything makes it better or worse"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0009",
      "speaker_id": "person_3",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 74.6,
      "end_seconds": 81.95,
      "duration_seconds": 7.35,
      "text": "Honestly, all the time. It's moderate, honestly. Sorry, I know I'm rambling a bit."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0010",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 83.55,
      "end_seconds": 86.47,
      "duration_seconds": 2.92,
      "text": "is there anything else with it?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0011",
      "speaker_id": "person_3",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 87.76,
      "end_seconds": 92.11,
      "duration_seconds": 4.35,
      "text": "It usually comes with constipation then loose stools."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0012",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 93.48,
      "end_seconds": 98.98,
      "duration_seconds": 5.5,
      "text": "a few quick ones: urinary symptoms, weight loss or blood in the stool?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0013",
      "speaker_id": "person_3",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 99.84,
      "end_seconds": 102.39,
      "duration_seconds": 2.55,
      "text": "no, I'd have said so"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0014",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 102.94,
      "end_seconds": 108.72,
      "duration_seconds": 5.78,
      "text": "I see go ahead. Anything with your nerves like weakness or numbness?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0015",
      "speaker_id": "person_3",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 110.64,
      "end_seconds": 112.07,
      "duration_seconds": 1.43,
      "text": "nothing odd there"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0016",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 117.24,
      "end_seconds": 120.1,
      "duration_seconds": 2.86,
      "text": "any breathing difficulties apart from this?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0017",
      "speaker_id": "person_3",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 121.35,
      "end_seconds": 123.87,
      "duration_seconds": 2.52,
      "text": "no you know nothing there"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0018",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 137.61,
      "end_seconds": 141.68,
      "duration_seconds": 4.07,
      "text": "Anything in your past medical history I should know?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0019",
      "speaker_id": "person_3",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 142.9,
      "end_seconds": 147.77,
      "duration_seconds": 4.87,
      "text": "I've had an irregular heartbeat for two years now"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0020",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 149.04,
      "end_seconds": 154.78,
      "duration_seconds": 5.74,
      "text": "yes. Tell me about your routine, work, habits, that sort of thing"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0021",
      "speaker_id": "person_3",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 155.75,
      "end_seconds": 172.43,
      "duration_seconds": 16.68,
      "text": "I only drink at family occasions. No, I've never smoked in my life. I look after my grandchildren most days. I grab fast food at lunch most days. I live with my elderly mother"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0022",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 173.95,
      "end_seconds": 178.45,
      "duration_seconds": 4.5,
      "text": "has anything ever caused you a reaction? I mean any allergies"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0023",
      "speaker_id": "person_3",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 179.19,
      "end_seconds": 182.46,
      "duration_seconds": 3.27,
      "text": "I don't think I have any no."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0024",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 185.0,
      "end_seconds": 187.37,
      "duration_seconds": 2.37,
      "text": "Have you had any previous surgeries?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0025",
      "speaker_id": "person_3",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 187.95,
      "end_seconds": 189.08,
      "duration_seconds": 1.13,
      "text": "no, never"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0026",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "NURSE",
      "start_seconds": 190.7,
      "end_seconds": 197.41,
      "duration_seconds": 6.71,
      "text": "okay so the vitals from earlier. Temperature is 38.6 degrees BP is 119 over 79 pulse 100."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0027",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 199.45,
      "end_seconds": 200.25,
      "duration_seconds": 0.8,
      "text": "Okay noted."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0028",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 202.89,
      "end_seconds": 207.12,
      "duration_seconds": 4.23,
      "text": "Now I'm going to do a short physical check."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0029",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 208.65,
      "end_seconds": 210.74,
      "duration_seconds": 2.09,
      "text": "hold that for a second"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0030",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 220.4,
      "end_seconds": 225.42,
      "duration_seconds": 5.02,
      "text": "It is tender in the lower left with no guarding or rigidity."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0031",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 228.82,
      "end_seconds": 230.55,
      "duration_seconds": 1.73,
      "text": "All finished thank you."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0032",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 237.56,
      "end_seconds": 244.33,
      "duration_seconds": 6.77,
      "text": "from what you've told me and and what I found, this looks most like acute diverticulitis"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0033",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 263.11,
      "end_seconds": 288.75,
      "duration_seconds": 25.64,
      "text": "I'll request blood tests, it'll help with abdominal pain. The result will help us decide whether anything more is needed. I'd like to arrange a CT scan for left iliac fossa pain. I'm going to put you on co-amoxiclav, 625 milligrams, three times a day, five days. That should help with diverticulitis"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0034",
      "speaker_id": "person_3",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 290.49,
      "end_seconds": 292.44,
      "duration_seconds": 1.95,
      "text": "Fine, I'll begin it."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0035",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 293.84,
      "end_seconds": 317.63,
      "duration_seconds": 23.79,
      "text": "Drink plenty and start with a light diet. If you smoke this is a good moment to think about stopping and we can help you with that. If the symptoms get worse or you feel really unwell please come to the emergency department. Let's plan a check in one week. Have I covered everything you wanted?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0036",
      "speaker_id": "person_3",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 318.14,
      "end_seconds": 319.7,
      "duration_seconds": 1.56,
      "text": "that's clear, thanks"
    }
  ]
}